# React patterns

## Components

- Default export functional components: `export default function ComponentName({ ... })`.
- Colocate by feature: `components/<feature>/`, pages in `pages/`, pure logic in `lib/`, static content in `data/`.
- Reuse shared UI primitives (`ActionButton`, `StatChip`, etc.) before inventing new button/chip patterns.
- Use `type="button"` explicitly on non-submit buttons.

## State and routing

- Keep page-level state in pages; pass callbacks down (`onFieldChange`, `onLevelChange`).
- Derive display values from source data + level/config — avoid duplicated editable state when the UI is read-only.
- Use React Router `Link` for navigation; wrap with transition helpers only when view transitions are intentional.

## Props and accessibility basics

- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` + `title` (see `ActionButton`).
- Expandable sections: `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`.
- Hidden/inert panels: `aria-hidden` + `inert` when content must not be focusable.
- Prefer `<button>` for actions; use `<a href>` only for real navigation.

## JSX style

- Tailwind for layout/spacing utilities; semantic/visual tokens in CSS classes (e.g. `bf-btn-primary`, `hero-action-btn`).
- Do not mix ad-hoc inline styles when a CSS class or token already exists.
